          "heading": "Luke Fitzgerald tips Sam Prendergast ahead of Ciaran Frawley for Argentina",
          "body": "Fitzgerald, a 34-times capped Ireland winger and 2009 Lions winger, rates Sam Prendergast as 'a nose in front' of Ciaran Frawley, citing his attacking play and defensive improvement despite kicking figures that have not been spectacular. He also floats Cian Prendergast for the back row with Caelan Doris absent, and argues Frawley's week-in, week-out Connacht form makes him valuable with the World Cup looming."
