          "kicker": "Injury update",
          "heading": "Dafydd Jenkins joins Wales camp with knee issue, Exeter expect no long-term problem",
          "body": "Wales lock Dafydd Jenkins has gone into camp for Saturday's match against Japan, with Exeter handing his medical care to the international staff. Jenkins missed Exeter's 31-28 defeat to Harlequins and was also absent from Wales' summer programme through injury. Scans showed bone bruising and some swelling on a piece of cartilage, and Exeter director of rugby Rob Baxter says they do not expect a long-term problem. Steve Tandy's squad includes 14 England-based players, and Jenkins is one of the Exeter contingent he will be relying on."
        },
