          "heading": "Joe Schmidt, ex-Wallabies boss, says 'a lot at stake' as Nations resumes",
          "body": "The former Australia head coach left the role after the Southern Hemisphere Series this summer, and he is now weighing up the wider picture as the inaugural Nations Championship resumes. Speaking to RTÉ Radio 1, Schmidt said \"I think there's a lot at stake for the game,\" and argued that the tournament could draw fans into taking sides. Australia's share of that stake comes at the end of the month, when North v South finals will decide the final standings across both hemispheres, a format Schmidt says he is looking forward to."
